:4287224861":"894508ccaae8179194ece824fac527c9456b27ef","review:5538575879":"894508ccaae8179194ece824fac527c9456b27ef"},"parent":"7dd16342f79e84e8744eb38283b11a0386197355","patch_sha256":"0b3f7357df3d17eb9d6e7d277ad976867dc642a31bf5e2deff1ecb20a81970c9","tree":"3435fef61bbfbf5c3f1033be49858525c8ac222d"},"confirmed_at":1792093804,"effect":"push","generation":1,"request_id":"1234836813764447bea2e5cebe4d3567","sha":"894508ccaae8179194ece824fac527c9456b27ef"}],"reason":"pending_fresh_trusted_personal_acceptance","report":{"artifact_id":12001528692,"candidate":{"bundle_sha256":"38eecf6c11d341d06d33ca733f7cf5f37c5b3777a478d5d1ddb29ad431ea03e6","changed":true,"changed_paths":[".github/scripts/instrumentations.sh","instrumentation/couchbase/couchbase-3.2/javaagent/build.gradle.kts","instrumentation/couchbase/couchbase-3.2/javaagent/src/version343Test/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/couchbase/v3_2/CouchbaseExceptionSignalTest.java"],"commit":"894508ccaae8179194ece824fac527c9456b27ef","commits":[{"changed_paths":[".github/scripts/instrumentations.sh","instrumentation/couchbase/couchbase-3.2/javaagent/build.gradle.kts","instrumentation/couchbase/couchbase-3.2/javaagent/src/version343Test/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/couchbase/v3_2/CouchbaseExceptionSignalTest.java"],"commit":"894508ccaae8179194ece824fac527c9456b27ef","parent":"7dd16342f79e84e8744eb38283b11a0386197355","patch_sha256":"0b3f7357df3d17eb9d6e7d277ad976867dc642a31bf5e2deff1ecb20a81970c9","subject":"Test Couchbase exception signals with the installed agent","tree":"3435fef61bbfbf5c3f1033be49858525c8ac222d"}],"cumulative_patch_sha256":"0b3f7357df3d17eb9d6e7d277ad976867dc642a31bf5e2deff1ecb20a81970c9","finding_commits":{"inline:4287224861":"894508ccaae8179194ece824fac527c9456b27ef","review:5538575879":"894508ccaae8179194ece824fac527c9456b27ef"},"parent":"7dd16342f79e84e8744eb38283b11a0386197355","patch_sha256":"0b3f7357df3d17eb9d6e7d277ad976867dc642a31bf5e2deff1ecb20a81970c9","tree":"3435fef61bbfbf5c3f1033be49858525c8ac222d"},"dispositions":{"findings":[{"analysis":"Added installed-agent coverage in the existing SDK 3.4.3 suite. A real asynchronous get times out against an unavailable local endpoint and the SDK invokes RequestSpan.recordException through its normal completion path. Default, logs, and logs/dup run in separate JVMs wired into check, with span-event selection, WARN exception attributes, logger scope/schema, and Couchbase span correlation asserted. The overview and inline finding describe the same coverage gap.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"review:5538575879"},{"analysis":"CouchbaseExceptionSignalTest constructs ClusterEnvironment with the installed agent, rather than manually supplying a tracer or logger. It performs a failing SDK 3.4.3 get, checks the SDK-provided CompletionException and its timeout cause, asserts the operation span exception selection, and verifies exactly one WARN db.client.operation.exception log with standard exception attributes, com.couchbase.client.jvm scope, the 1.44.0 schema, and the operation span context. The default suite and filtered logs/logs-dup JVM variants pass and are dependencies of check. Both non-default event profiles are registered and verified in metadata collection.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"inline:4287224861"}],"input_identity":{},"outcome":"fixes","request_digest":"ac2fce4927f903b4af103b6f427bdb0317af5bc50a38d07e223ac19aa676a52f","schema":2},"download_sha256":"981459f8bd73aa838199d8fb4c6c769256a81f7ddf9ed962f71ab2cb857c7291","frozen_sha":"7dd16342f79e84e8744eb38283b11a0386197355","pr":20621,"publication_eligible":false,"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","request_digest":"ac2fce4927f903b4af103b6f427bdb0317af5bc50a38d07e223ac19aa676a52f","request_id":"1234836813764447bea2e5cebe4d3567","run_attempt":1,"run_id":38792406399,"schema":2,"scope":"Structural/Git verification only. No target code or tests are executed.","server_artifact_digest":"sha256:981459f8bd73aa838199d8fb4c6c769256a81f7ddf9ed962f71ab2cb857c7291","verification":"verified","verification_run":{"attempt":1,"id":38796802540},"workflow_revision":"1a211828aa1a2b731f5e9140623b5945a0dbdb6d"},"request":{"authorized_actor_id":218610,"baseline_review_ids":[5537493320,5537557129,5537940618,5538021137,5538063924,5538139866,5538509888,5538575879],"budgets":{"max_iterations":5,"propagation_seconds":120,"retention_days":14,"worker_timeout_minutes":30},"commit_author":{"id":218610,"login":"trask"},"findings":[{"body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### \ud83d\udfe1 Changes recommended\n\nException-signal behavior needs installed-agent coverage exercising logger initialization and the Couchbase SDK exception callback together.\n\n<details open>\n<summary><strong>1 open finding</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Add agent-backed coverage for logger modes and exception span logging](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/20621#discussion_r4287224861) \u00b7 New\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>What changed in this PR</strong></summary>\n\nUpdates Couchbase 3.x instrumentation to honor exception-signal settings while preserving span events by default.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Adds correlated WARN exception logs for `logs` and `logs/dup`.\n- Wires exception loggers into Couchbase tracer factories.\n- Adds unit tests and separate JVM variants for signal selection.\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| instrumentation/\u200bcouchbase/\u200bcouchbase-common-3.0/\u200bjavaagent/\u200bsrc/\u200bmain/\u200bjava/\u200bio/\u200bopentelemetry/\u200bjavaagent/\u200binstrumentation/\u200bcouchbase/\u200bcommon/\u200bv3_0/\u200bCouchbaseTracer.java | Passes the exception logger to spans. |\r\n| instrumentation/\u200bcouchbase/\u200bcouchbase-common-3.0/\u200bjavaagent/\u200bsrc/\u200bmain/\u200bjava/\u200bio/\u200bopentelemetry/\u200bjavaagent/\u200binstrumentation/\u200bcouchbase/\u200bcommon/\u200bv3_0/\u200bCouchbaseSpan.java | Selects exception events, logs, or both. |\r\n| instrumentation/\u200bcouchbase/\u200bcouchbase-common-3.0/\u200bjavaagent-unit-tests/\u200bsrc/\u200btest/\u200bjava/\u200bio/\u200bopentelemetry/\u200bjavaagent/\u200binstrumentation/\u200bcouchbase/\u200bcommon/\u200bv3_0/\u200bCouchbaseTracerTest.java | Tests signal selection and correlation. |\r\n| instrumentation/\u200bcouchbase/\u200bcouchbase-common-3.0/\u200bjavaagent-unit-tests/\u200bbuild.gradle.kts | Adds logging-mode test variants. |\r\n| instrumentation/\u200bcouchbase/\u200bcouchbase-3.2/\u200bjavaagent/\u200bsrc/\u200bmain/\u200bjava/\u200bio/\u200bopentelemetry/\u200bjavaagent/\u200binstrumentation/\u200bcouchbase/\u200bv3_2/\u200bCouchbaseRequestTracer.java | Creates the 3.2 exception logger. |\r\n| instrumentation/\u200bcouchbase/\u200bcouchbase-3.1/\u200bjavaagent/\u200bsrc/\u200bmain/\u200bjava/\u200bio/\u200bopentelemetry/\u200bjavaagent/\u200binstrumentation/\u200bcouchbase/\u200bv3_1/\u200bCouchbaseRequestTracer.java | Creates matching tracers and loggers. |\r\n| instrumentation/\u200bcouchbase/\u200bcouchbase-3.1/\u200bjavaagent/\u200bsrc/\u200bmain/\u200bjava/\u200bio/\u200bopentelemetry/\u200bjavaagent/\u200binstrumentation/\u200bcouchbase/\u200bv3_1/\u200bCouchbaseEnvironmentInstrumentation.java | Delegates telemetry initialization to the factory. |\r\n| instrumentation/\u200bcouchbase/\u200bcouchbase-3.0/\u200bjavaagent/\u200bsrc/\u200bmain/\u200bjava/\u200bio/\u200bopentelemetry/\u200bjavaagent/\u200binstrumentation/\u200bcouchbase/\u200bv3_0/\u200bCouchbaseRequestTracer.java | Creates the 3.0 exception logger. |\r\n| instrumentation/\u200bcouchbase/\u200bcouchbase-3.0/\u200bjavaagent/\u200bsrc/\u200bmain/\u200bjava/\u200bio/\u200bopentelemetry/\u200bjavaagent/\u200binstrumentation/\u200bcouchbase/\u200bv3_0/\u200bCouchbaseEnvironmentInstrumentation.java | Delegates telemetry initialization to the factory. |\n</details>\n\n\ud83e\udde0 **Review effort:** Balanced\n\n---\n\n\ud83d\udca1 <a href=\"/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5538575879","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5538575879},{"body":"[Testing] The `logs` and `logs/dup` tasks only run helper tests with a manually supplied logger. The installed-agent Couchbase tests do not exercise these modes or assert exception logs, so the new logger factory and SDK `RequestSpan.recordException` callback are not tested together. Add an agent-backed failing operation on a supported SDK version that invokes the callback, covering default, `logs`, and `logs/dup` in separate JVMs wired into `check`. Assert span-event selection and the WARN exception log's scope and Couchbase span correlation.","comment_commit_id":"7dd16342f79e84e8744eb38283b11a0386197355","comment_id":4287224861,"key":"inline:4287224861","kind":"inline","line":45,"original_commit_id":"7dd16342f79e84e8744eb38283b11a0386197355","original_line":45,"path":"instrumentation/couchbase/couchbase-3.2/javaagent/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/couchbase/v3_2/CouchbaseRequestTracer.java","review_commit_id":"7dd16342f79e84e8744eb38283b11a0386197355","review_id":5538575879,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-15T19:11:53Z","root_author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"thread_context":[{"author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"body_hash":"1f8c533990b45cfb2930eec99627a93e3e736b7a903f5712dda765d530c51a91","id":4287224861,"parent":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-15T19:11:53Z"}],"thread_id":"PRRT_kwDODJKVX86s7Y7Y"}],"frozen_at":1792091671,"frozen_at_iso":"2026-10-15T19:14:31Z","frozen_sha":"7dd16342f79e84e8744eb38283b11a0386197355","head_ref":"copilot/finish-couchbase-exception-recording","head_repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","head_repo_id":210933087,"input_mode":"direct","launch_run":{"actor_id":218610,"attempt":1,"id":38792236795},"loop_kind":"copilot_review","metadata":{"body":"<!--\nCHANGELOG.md is generated from merged pull requests. Do not add an entry unless this PR introduces\na deprecation or breaking change.\n-->\n\nCouchbase 3.x exception recording now follows `otel.semconv.exception.signal.preview`: unset preserves span events, `logs` emits exception logs, and `logs/dup` emits both.\n\n- **Log behavior** \u2014 Emits `db.client.operation.exception` at `WARN` severity with standard exception attributes, correlated to the Couchbase span.\n- **Example** \u2014 Set `otel.semconv.exception.signal.preview=logs` to emit logs only.","title":"Honor exception signal settings for Couchbase 3.x"},"mode":"publish","pr":20621,"pr_author_id":198982749,"protocol":"git-candidate-v1","publication":{"auth_mode":"fine_grained_pat","authorized_actor_id":218610,"authorized_at":1792091674,"generation":1,"max_pipelines":5,"phase":"b0265061d6414c7eae538d9951494df8","profile":"git-candidate-v1","required_checks":[]},"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","repo_id":210933087,"request_id":"123483681376444